From 1e95d685140923f0ab33d7d0051548e065736ea4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeremy Barnum <prefer not to supply>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 11:38:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] A time scale for Simulator testing, behind a build flag

Simulator testing only: with SIMULATED_TIME_SCALE_ENABLED set and
SPORTMODE_TIME_SCALE=N in the app's environment, the waits that follow
the sensor's 5-minute cadence are divided by N: the 4.2-minute loop
limit on the phone and the watch, the take-back's settle limit, the
watch-contact window, the silent-watch threshold, grace, warning marks
and tick tolerance, the phone's own-glucose freshness window, and the
unconfirmed-loan timer. Real latencies (answer waits, resends, leases)
are not scaled. 1 on a device, without the flag, and under XCTest.
For the production line's Simulator tests; never merged into it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 Loop/Managers/DeviceDataManager.swift         |  4 ++--
 Loop/Managers/PodLoanPhoneController.swift    | 18 +++++++--------
 LoopCore/LoopCoreConstants.swift              | 22 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../StockLoop/WatchLoopManager.swift          |  6 ++---
 4 files changed, 36 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

